# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ai-validation/liodon — ignore rules
#
# This lab is a validation harness, not the ERP. Its rule is simple: commit the
# code and the documentation, never the downloaded weights and never the
# generated output.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- The real model -------------------------------------------------------
# best.onnx is NOT committed. It is the publisher's artifact (CC-BY-NC-4.0,
# ~10.1 MB) and it is fetched and SHA-256 verified on the machine that runs the
# validation, by scripts/download_liodon.py. Shipping a copy in git would mean
# nobody could tell whether the bytes they ran were the published ones.
model/*.onnx
model/*.pt

# --- Generated test artifacts --------------------------------------------
# Rebuilt on demand by scripts/make_standin_onnx.py. Synthetic; never a real
# model, and never named best.onnx.
input/_synthetic_panoramic_test.png

# --- Run output -----------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerated by every run. Keeping these out means `git status` stays clean
# after you run the validation locally.
output/*
!output/.gitkeep
!output/NOTE.txt

# --- Run logs -------------------------------------------------------------
logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/

# --- Editors / OS ---------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
